### `core-CONTRACT-001` Typed chain model, global validation, watched changes

❌ not yet implemented. `catalyst-core` exposes a single message
protocol (defined once, before any host exists) covering: (1) a typed
chain model connecting work items → dev artifacts → rules → rules of
rules, built from a full reparse of the corpus; (2) global validation
that runs on every reparse, never incrementally — orphaned artifacts,
rules without meta-rule backing, ID reuse, and dangling references are
inherently cross-cutting checks, not per-file ones; (3) a file watcher
that debounces/coalesces changes in a 150–200ms trailing window and
uses single-flight cancellation, so a change landing mid-parse aborts
and restarts rather than queuing. Targeted by `REQ-000001`.

